.TH BAUD 1 "" "baud 0.1.3" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
baud \- A fast, feature\-rich, GPU\-accelerated, cross\-platform terminal emulator
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B baud
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] [\fICOMMAND\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
A fast, feature\-rich, GPU\-accelerated, cross\-platform terminal emulator
With no arguments, baud asks the session daemon to open a tab. The commands and options below are resolved before the graphical backend starts, so they also work in a broken graphical session.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fBupdate\fR
Update Baud to the latest release
.TP
\fBversion\fR
Print the installed Baud version
.TP
\fBmcp\fR
Speak MCP over stdio to a running Baud instance
.TP
\fBhelp\fR
Show this help message
.TP
\fB\-e <command> [args...]\fR
Execute command and its arguments in the PTY
.TP
\fB\-\-working\-directory <dir>\fR
Set the initial working directory for the child process
.TP
\fB\-\-title <text>\fR
Set the initial window title
.TP
\fB\-\-app\-id <id>\fR
Set the Wayland app_id / X11 WM_CLASS instance
.TP
\fB\-\-hold\fR
Keep the window open after the command exits
.TP
\fB\-\-config <path>\fR
Load config from this file instead of the default search path
.TP
\fB\-o <key=value>\fR
Override a config key (repeatable); invalid keys are skipped
.TP
\fB\-\-window\-size <COLSxROWS>\fR
Set the initial window size in terminal cells
.TP
\fB\-\-maximized\fR
Start the window maximized
.TP
\fB\-\-fullscreen\fR
Start the window in borderless fullscreen
.TP
\fB\-\-server\fR
Run the session daemon in the foreground
.TP
\fB\-\-new\-instance\fR
Open a GUI that does not talk to the daemon
.TP
\fB\-v, \-\-version\fR
Print the installed Baud version
.TP
\fB\-h, \-\-help\fR
Show this help message
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/baud/config.toml
or ~/.config/baud/config.toml on Linux; %APPDATA%\\baud\\config.toml on Windows.
.TP
.I ./baud.toml
Working\-directory fallback, checked if the file above is not found.
.PP
If \-\-config is given, that file replaces this search path and is the one watched for hot\-reload. CLI \-o overrides are re\-applied after every reload.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.I TERM
Forced to xterm-256color in the child process.
.TP
.I COLORTERM
Forced to truecolor in the child process.
.SH SEE ALSO
Full documentation: \fIhttps://github.com/KarloZ7715/Baud\fR
